     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Julie,<div><br></div><div>No, you do not need multiple columns for the variable, sex, when performing procD.lm.  To perform MANOVA to test for differences between sexes and to use procD.lm to do this are appropriate, but it sounds like you made a mistake when setting up the analysis.  To say it “does not work” with no details how it did not work makes it impossible to diagnose the problem.  However, likely issues could be with the format of your variable (sex), how you set up your model formula in procD.lm, missing data, whether you use a data frame in the set up, and possibly a mismatch in the number of specimens between the two data sets. The procD.lm help file should help resolve these issues.</div><div><br></div><div>I also recommend that next time you post an issue, you include your procD.lm coding, like you did for the gpagen, and the error message returned.  It will make it easier for someone to provide assistance.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers!</div><div>Mike<br><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Jun 26, 2018, at 7:11 AM, Julie Lorenzen &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">julielo...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Dear all,<u></u><u></u></span></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Sorry for the, maybe, basic question. I am still new to the geomorph package. I am trying to do some GMM on my dataset containing 3D skull data obtained using a microscribe. My main goal is to test whether there are differences between male and female skulls.<span> </span><u></u><u></u></span></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I have uploaded the data using the readland.tps function<span> </span><u></u><u></u></span></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;text-indent:65.2pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">mydata &lt;- readland.tps(&quot;PB_skulls.TPS&quot;, specID =&quot;ID&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">A separate document contains the classifiers, where I have a column containing the IDs used and another called Sex where they either are males or females.  <u></u><u></u></span></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;text-indent:65.2pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">classifier &lt;- read.csv(&quot;CnSex.csv&quot;, header=T, row.names=1, sep=&#39;;&#39;)<u></u><u></u></span></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I have performed a gpa using the gpagen function and a PCA using the plotTangentSpace function.<span> </span><u></u><u></u></span></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">            gpa &lt;- gpagen(mydata, Proj=TRUE, ProcD = TRUE, curves = NULL, surfaces = NULL)<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">            plotTangentSpace(gpa$coords)<u></u><u></u></span></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Next I want to test whether the skulls for females and males are significantly different or not. However, I have trouble figuring out if I am doing this correctly and if this is the right approach to do this.<span> </span><u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">From what I know I think I need to use a MANOVA test. I have tried using the procD.lm function, however this does not work. I suspect that it may be because I have only one column in the classifier file containing both males and females under the category “Sex”. Should I make them separate columns? Or is this simply not the right approach to do it, and how should I approach it instead?<u></u><u></u></span></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Thank you in advance,<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Julie <u></u><u></u></span></div></div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><br></div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none;float:none;display:inline!important\">--<span> </span></span><br style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none;float:none;display:inline!important\">You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;geomorph R package&quot; group.</span><br style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none;float:none;display:inline!important\">To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to<span> </span></span><a href style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;l